The first final-browser probe incorrectly required all eight legacy Markdown aliases in HTML. It failed the first case before navigation. canonical::html does not read aliases: HTML uses the seven emitted semantic Section IDs. This is an incorrect test assumption, not a successful display/navigation run or a change to production. The corrected script tests seven HTML semantic targets and the real cross-page link; GitHub separately tests eight legacy aliases and seven semantic IDs. Earlier user-facing claim that old aliases were present in both formats was explicitly corrected.
